      out.write("              Beryl Cook is one of Britain’s most talented and amusing artists\r\n");
      out.write("              .Beryl’s pictures feature women of all shapes and sizes enjoying\r\n");
      out.write("              themselves .Born between the two world wars, Beryl Cook eventually\r\n");
      out.write("              left Kendrick School in Reading at the age of 15, where she went\r\n");
      out.write("              to secretarial school and then into an insurance office. After\r\n");
      out.write("              moving to London and then Hampton, she eventually married her next\r\n");
      out.write("              door neighbour from Reading, John Cook. He was an officer in the\r\n");
      out.write("              Merchant Navy and after he left the sea in 1956, they bought a pub\r\n");
      out.write("              for a year before John took a job in Southern Rhodesia with a\r\n");
      out.write("              motor company. Beryl bought their young son a box of watercolours,\r\n");
      out.write("              and when showing him how to use it, she decided that she herself\r\n");
      out.write("              quite enjoyed painting. John subsequently bought her a child’s\r\n");
      out.write("              painting set for her birthday and it was with this that she\r\n");
      out.write("              produced her first significant work, a half-length portrait of a\r\n");
      out.write("              dark-skinned lady with a vacant expression and large drooping\r\n");
      out.write("              breasts. It was aptly named ‘Hangover’ by Beryl’s husband and\r\n");
      out.write("            </p>\r\n");
